==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|hasinscharte}}. {{surface analysis|de|Hase|t1=hare|-n-|Scharte|t3=notch}}. So called because of the similarity to the outer form of a hare’s lip. Compare already {{cog|ang|hærsceard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈhaːzənˌʃaʁtə/|[ˈhaː.zn̩ˌʃaʁ.tə]|[-zən-]|[ˌʃaɐ̯-]|[-ˌʃaː-]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Hasenscharte.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# [[cleft lip]], [[harelip]]
#: {{syn|de|Lippenspalte}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|de||Hasenscharte}} is the common term among the general population, but {{m|de||Lippenspalte}} is used in medical contexts and is considered [[politically correct]].

